The insights.ts command has 27% log density (44 console.log calls in 148 lines).

All logs are intentional terminal output, NOT debug logging. The issue is that formatting logic is mixed with command logic.

FIX: Extract formatting to a separate function that returns a string.

Pattern to follow:
```typescript
// Before (current):
function runInsights() {
  console.log(chalk.bold.cyan('═'.repeat(64)));
  console.log(chalk.bold.cyan('  YOUR SPIRAL PATTERNS'));
  // ... 40 more console.log
}

// After:
function formatInsightsOutput(data): string {
  const lines = [];
  lines.push(chalk.bold.cyan('═'.repeat(64)));
  lines.push(chalk.bold.cyan('  YOUR SPIRAL PATTERNS'));
  return lines.join('\n');
}

function runInsights() {
  const output = formatInsightsOutput(data);
  console.log(output);
}
```

Files affected: src/commands/insights.ts

Acceptance criteria:
- [ ] Create formatInsightsOutput() function
- [ ] Move all console.log calls into lines.push() pattern
- [ ] Single console.log(output) in command handler
- [ ] Verify output unchanged: npm run build && node dist/cli.js insights
